/-!
# C⋆-dynamical systems

A **C⋆-dynamical system** `(A, G, α)` is a C⋆-algebra `A`, a topological group `G` and an action
of `G` on `A` by ⋆-automorphisms, continuous in the point-norm topology: `g ↦ α g a` is continuous
for every `a`. It is spelled as a continuous homomorphism `α : G →ₜ* (A ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] A)`, the
⋆-automorphisms carrying the topology of pointwise convergence
(`QuantumSystem.Analysis.CStarAlgebra.StarAlgEquiv`), in which they form a topological
group. An additive group `V`, such as the time axis `ℝ`, acts by a continuous additive character
`α : ContinuousAddChar V (A ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] A)`, with `α (s + t) = α s * α t`; it is the continuous
homomorphism `α.toContinuousMonoidHom` from `Multiplicative V`
(`QuantumSystem.ForMathlib.Topology.Algebra.ContinuousAddChar`). No separate name is given to
`G →ₜ* (A ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] A)`: Mathlib's `ContinuousMonoidHom` is the object.

Examples:

* the inner action `u ↦ (x ↦ u x u⋆)` of the unitary group of `A`
  (`Unitary.continuousConjStarAlgAut`), whose fixed points are the centre of `A`
  (`StarAlgEquiv.fixedPoints_conjStarAlgAut`);
* a group `G` with continuous inversion acting continuously on a space `X`, on the continuous
  functions `C(X, ℂ)` by `(g · f) x = f (g⁻¹ • x)` (`ContinuousMap.smulStarAlgAut`), a
  C⋆-dynamical system for a compact `X`; its fixed points are the `G`-invariant functions, the
  constants for a transitive action (`ContinuousMap.fixedPoints_smulStarAlgAut_of_isPretransitive`);
* a symmetry group of a faithful local net acting continuously on its quasi-local algebra
  (`GradedLocalNet.Automorphism.quasiLocalCStarDynamicalSystem`).

`G` need not be a topological group for the statements below: none of them uses the continuity of the
multiplication of `G`, and only `ContinuousMap.smulStarAlgAut` uses that of its inversion.

The fixed points `A^α = {a | ∀ g, α g a = a}` of an action by ⋆-automorphisms form a ⋆-subalgebra,
defined without topology: a non-unital one for a ⋆-algebra that need not be unital
(`StarAlgEquiv.nonUnitalFixedPoints`), whose carrier is Mathlib's `MulAction.fixedPoints` of the
monoid of the `α g` acting on `A` by `StarAlgEquiv.applyMulAction`; and for a unital `A` the unital
one (`StarAlgEquiv.fixedPoints`), whose underlying subalgebra is Mathlib's `FixedPoints.subalgebra`
and whose underlying non-unital ⋆-subalgebra is the former by definition
(`StarAlgEquiv.fixedPoints_toNonUnitalStarSubalgebra`), so that every statement about it is
derived from the non-unital one. It is closed as soon as `A` is a Hausdorff
topological ⋆-algebra and every `α g` is continuous (`StarAlgEquiv.isClosed_fixedPoints`): in a
C⋆-algebra, where every ⋆-automorphism is isometric, so that `A^α` is a C⋆-algebra in its own right;
in the σ-weak copy of a von Neumann algebra, for an action by σ-weakly continuous automorphisms. A
⋆-automorphism restricts to a ⋆-subalgebra it maps onto itself (`StarAlgEquiv.restrict`), and an
action to every invariant ⋆-subalgebra (`StarAlgEquiv.restrictHom`).

## Main definitions

* `StarAlgEquiv.nonUnitalFixedPoints α`, `StarAlgEquiv.fixedPoints α` — the ⋆-subalgebra `A^α` of
  the points fixed by every `α g`, non-unital and unital.
* `StarAlgEquiv.involutionHom e he` — the action of `ℤ₂` generated by an involutive ⋆-automorphism
  `e`, whose fixed points are those of `e` (`StarAlgEquiv.mem_fixedPoints_involutionHom`).
* `StarAlgEquiv.average α` — the average `a ↦ (1 / |G|) ∑ g, α g a` of the orbit of `a` under an
  action of a finite group of invertible order, Mathlib's `Representation.averageMap` of the
  underlying linear representation `StarAlgEquiv.toRepresentation α`.
* `StarAlgEquiv.restrict e s h h'` — the restriction of a ⋆-automorphism `e` to a ⋆-subalgebra `s`
  that `e` maps onto itself.
* `StarAlgEquiv.restrictHom α s h` — the restriction of `α` to an invariant ⋆-subalgebra `s`.
* `ContinuousMap.smulStarAlgAut G X` — the action of `G` on `C(X, ℂ)` induced by a
  continuous action on `X`.

## Main results

* `StarAlgEquiv.isClosed_nonUnitalFixedPoints`, `StarAlgEquiv.isClosed_fixedPoints` — `A^α` is
  closed for an action by continuous ⋆-automorphisms of a Hausdorff topological ⋆-algebra;
  `StarAlgEquiv.instIsClosedNonUnitalFixedPoints`, `StarAlgEquiv.instIsClosedFixedPoints` — in a
  C⋆-algebra, so that `A^α` is a C⋆-algebra.
* `StarAlgEquiv.isProj_average` — the average is a projection onto `A^α`.
* **`StarAlgEquiv.fixedPoints_conjStarAlgAut`** — the fixed points of the inner action of the
  unitary group are the centre.
* **`StarAlgEquiv.mem_nonUnitalFixedPoints_iff_of_dense`**,
  **`StarAlgEquiv.mem_fixedPoints_iff_of_dense`** — the fixed points of an action continuous for the
  topology of pointwise convergence are the points fixed by any dense subset of `G`.
* `ContinuousMap.mem_fixedPoints_smulStarAlgAut`,
  `ContinuousMap.fixedPoints_smulStarAlgAut_of_isPretransitive` — the fixed points of the
  action on `C(X, ℂ)` are the invariant functions; for a transitive action, the constants.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace StarAlgEquiv

section NonUnitalFixedPoints

variable {G R A : Type*} [Monoid G] [CommSemiring R] [NonUnitalNonAssocSemiring A] [Module R A]
  [Star A]

/-- The **fixed-point algebra** `A^α` of an action `α : G →* (A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A)` by ⋆-automorphisms of a
⋆-algebra `A` that need not be unital: the non-unital ⋆-subalgebra of the `G`-invariant elements.
Its carrier is Mathlib's `MulAction.fixedPoints` of the monoid `MonoidHom.mrange α` acting on `A`.
For a unital `A` it is the underlying non-unital ⋆-subalgebra of `StarAlgEquiv.fixedPoints`
(`StarAlgEquiv.fixedPoints_toNonUnitalStarSubalgebra`). -/
def nonUnitalFixedPoints (α : G →* (A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A)) : NonUnitalStarSubalgebra R A where
  carrier := MulAction.fixedPoints (MonoidHom.mrange α) A
  add_mem' ha hb g := by rw [Submonoid.smul_def, StarAlgEquiv.smul_def, map_add, ← StarAlgEquiv.smul_def,
    ← StarAlgEquiv.smul_def, ← Submonoid.smul_def, ← Submonoid.smul_def, ha g, hb g]
  zero_mem' g := map_zero (g : A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A)
  mul_mem' ha hb g := by rw [Submonoid.smul_def, StarAlgEquiv.smul_def, map_mul, ← StarAlgEquiv.smul_def,
    ← StarAlgEquiv.smul_def, ← Submonoid.smul_def, ← Submonoid.smul_def, ha g, hb g]
  smul_mem' r a ha g := by rw [Submonoid.smul_def, StarAlgEquiv.smul_def, map_smul,
    ← StarAlgEquiv.smul_def, ← Submonoid.smul_def, ha g]
  star_mem' ha g := by rw [Submonoid.smul_def, StarAlgEquiv.smul_def, map_star,
    ← StarAlgEquiv.smul_def, ← Submonoid.smul_def, ha g]

/-- A point is in `A^α` iff every `α g` fixes it. -/
@[simp] lemma mem_nonUnitalFixedPoints {α : G →* (A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A)} {a : A} :
    a ∈ nonUnitalFixedPoints α ↔ ∀ g, α g a = a := by
  change (∀ g : MonoidHom.mrange α, g • a = a) ↔ _
  simp [Submonoid.smul_def]

variable [TopologicalSpace A] [T2Space A]

/-- The fixed-point algebra of an action by continuous ⋆-automorphisms of a Hausdorff topological
⋆-algebra is closed. -/
lemma isClosed_nonUnitalFixedPoints (α : G →* (A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A)) (hα : ∀ g, Continuous (α g)) :
    IsClosed (nonUnitalFixedPoints α : Set A) := by
  have h : (nonUnitalFixedPoints α : Set A) = ⋂ g, {a | α g a = a} := by
    ext
    simp
  rw [h]
  exact isClosed_iInter fun g => isClosed_eq (hα g) continuous_id

/-- The fixed points of an action `α`, continuous for the topology of pointwise convergence on the
⋆-automorphisms of a Hausdorff topological ⋆-algebra, are the points fixed by `α g` for `g` in any
dense subset `S` of `G`: for each `a`, the `g` with `α g a = a` form a closed set, `g ↦ α g a` being
continuous. No compatibility of the topology of `G` with its multiplication is used. -/
lemma mem_nonUnitalFixedPoints_iff_of_dense [TopologicalSpace G] (α : G →ₜ* (A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A))
    {S : Set G} (hS : Dense S) {a : A} :
    a ∈ nonUnitalFixedPoints α.toMonoidHom ↔ ∀ g ∈ S, α g a = a := by
  rw [mem_nonUnitalFixedPoints]
  refine ⟨fun h g _ => h g, fun h g => ?_⟩
  have hc : IsClosed {g : G | α g a = a} :=
    isClosed_eq ((continuous_eval_const a).comp α.continuous) continuous_const
  have hsub : closure S ⊆ {g | α g a = a} := hc.closure_subset_iff.mpr fun g hg => h g hg
  exact hsub (hS.closure_eq ▸ Set.mem_univ g)

end NonUnitalFixedPoints

section Involution

variable {R A : Type*} [Add A] [Mul A] [SMul R A] [Star A]

/-- The **action of `ℤ₂`** generated by an involutive ⋆-automorphism `e`: the generator acts by `e`. -/
noncomputable def involutionHom (e : A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A) (he : e * e = 1) :
    Multiplicative (ZMod 2) →* (A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A) :=
  AddMonoidHom.toMultiplicativeLeft
    (ZMod.lift 2 ⟨zmultiplesHom (Additive (A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A)) (Additive.ofMul e), by
      change Additive.ofMul (e ^ (2 : ℤ)) = 0
      rw [zpow_two, he]
      rfl⟩)

/-- The generator of `ℤ₂` acts by `e`. -/
@[simp] lemma involutionHom_ofAdd_one (e : A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A) (he : e * e = 1) :
    involutionHom e he (Multiplicative.ofAdd 1) = e := by
  change Additive.toMul (ZMod.lift 2 _ ((1 : ℤ) : ZMod 2)) = e
  rw [ZMod.lift_coe]
  simp

end Involution

section FixedPoints

variable {G R A : Type*} [Monoid G] [CommSemiring R] [StarRing R] [Semiring A] [Algebra R A]
  [StarRing A] [StarModule R A]

/-- The **fixed-point algebra** `A^α` of an action `α : G →* (A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A)` by ⋆-automorphisms of a
unital ⋆-algebra: the ⋆-subalgebra of the `G`-invariant elements. Its underlying subalgebra is
Mathlib's `FixedPoints.subalgebra` for the monoid `MonoidHom.mrange α` of ⋆-automorphisms acting on
`A`; it is closed under the adjoint, each `α g` commuting with the adjoint. In a C⋆-algebra it is a C⋆-algebra
with the same unit. -/
def fixedPoints (α : G →* (A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A)) : StarSubalgebra R A where
  toSubalgebra := FixedPoints.subalgebra R A (MonoidHom.mrange α)
  star_mem' {a} ha g := by
    rw [Submonoid.smul_def, StarAlgEquiv.smul_def, map_star, ← StarAlgEquiv.smul_def,
      ← Submonoid.smul_def, ha g]

/-- The subalgebra underlying `A^α` is Mathlib's algebra of fixed points of the monoid
`MonoidHom.mrange α`. -/
lemma fixedPoints_toSubalgebra (α : G →* (A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A)) :
    (fixedPoints α).toSubalgebra = FixedPoints.subalgebra R A (MonoidHom.mrange α) :=
  rfl

/-- The non-unital ⋆-subalgebra underlying `A^α` is `StarAlgEquiv.nonUnitalFixedPoints α`. -/
lemma fixedPoints_toNonUnitalStarSubalgebra (α : G →* (A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A)) :
    (fixedPoints α).toNonUnitalStarSubalgebra = nonUnitalFixedPoints α :=
  rfl

/-- A point is in `A^α` iff every `α g` fixes it. -/
@[simp] lemma mem_fixedPoints {α : G →* (A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A)} {a : A} :
    a ∈ fixedPoints α ↔ ∀ g, α g a = a :=
  mem_nonUnitalFixedPoints

/-- The fixed points of the action of `ℤ₂` generated by an involutive ⋆-automorphism `e` are the
points fixed by `e`. -/
lemma mem_fixedPoints_involutionHom {e : A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A} {he : e * e = 1} {a : A} :
    a ∈ fixedPoints (involutionHom e he) ↔ e a = a := by
  rw [mem_fixedPoints]
  refine ⟨fun h => by simpa [involutionHom_ofAdd_one] using h (Multiplicative.ofAdd 1),
    fun h g => ?_⟩
  induction g using Multiplicative.rec with | ofAdd n => ?_
  fin_cases n
  · change (involutionHom e he 1) a = a
    simp
  · change (involutionHom e he (Multiplicative.ofAdd 1)) a = a
    rw [involutionHom_ofAdd_one]
    exact h

variable [TopologicalSpace A] [T2Space A]

/-- The fixed-point algebra of an action by continuous ⋆-automorphisms of a Hausdorff topological
⋆-algebra is closed (`StarAlgEquiv.isClosed_nonUnitalFixedPoints`). -/
lemma isClosed_fixedPoints (α : G →* (A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A)) (hα : ∀ g, Continuous (α g)) :
    IsClosed (fixedPoints α : Set A) :=
  isClosed_nonUnitalFixedPoints α hα

/-- The fixed points of an action `α`, continuous for the topology of pointwise convergence on the
⋆-automorphisms of a Hausdorff topological ⋆-algebra, are the points fixed by `α g` for `g` in any
dense subset `S` of `G` (`StarAlgEquiv.mem_nonUnitalFixedPoints_iff_of_dense`). For a C⋆-dynamical
system the topology of `A` is that of the norm; for a W⋆-dynamical system, the σ-weak topology. -/
lemma mem_fixedPoints_iff_of_dense [TopologicalSpace G] (α : G →ₜ* (A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A)) {S : Set G}
    (hS : Dense S) {a : A} : a ∈ fixedPoints α.toMonoidHom ↔ ∀ g ∈ S, α g a = a :=
  mem_nonUnitalFixedPoints_iff_of_dense α hS

end FixedPoints

section Average

variable {G R A : Type*} [Group G] [CommRing R] [Ring A] [Algebra R A] [StarRing A]

/-- The linear representation of `G` on `A` underlying an action by ⋆-automorphisms. -/
def toRepresentation (α : G →* (A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A)) : Representation R G A where
  toFun g := (α g).toAlgEquiv.toLinearMap
  map_one' := by ext; simp
  map_mul' g h := by ext; simp [StarAlgEquiv.mul_apply]

@[simp] lemma toRepresentation_apply (α : G →* (A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A)) (g : G) (a : A) :
    toRepresentation α g a = α g a :=
  rfl

variable [Fintype G] [Invertible (Fintype.card G : R)]

/-- The **average** `a ↦ (1 / |G|) ∑ g, α g a` of the orbit of `a` under an action of a finite group
whose order is invertible in `R`: Mathlib's `Representation.averageMap` of the underlying linear
representation, a projection onto the fixed-point algebra (`StarAlgEquiv.isProj_average`). -/
noncomputable abbrev average (α : G →* (A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A)) : A →ₗ[R] A :=
  (toRepresentation α).averageMap

lemma average_apply (α : G →* (A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A)) (a : A) :
    average α a = ⅟(Fintype.card G : R) • ∑ g, α g a := by
  simp [GroupAlgebra.average, map_sum]

variable [StarRing R] [StarModule R A]

/-- The average of `a` is fixed by the action (`Representation.averageMap_invariant`). -/
theorem average_mem_fixedPoints (α : G →* (A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A)) (a : A) : average α a ∈ fixedPoints α :=
  mem_fixedPoints.mpr fun g => (toRepresentation α).averageMap_invariant a g

/-- The average fixes the fixed points (`Representation.averageMap_id`). -/
theorem average_eq_self {α : G →* (A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A)} {a : A} (ha : a ∈ fixedPoints α) :
    average α a = a :=
  (toRepresentation α).averageMap_id a fun g => mem_fixedPoints.mp ha g

/-- **The average is a projection onto the fixed-point algebra.** -/
theorem isProj_average (α : G →* (A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A)) :
    LinearMap.IsProj (fixedPoints α).toSubalgebra.toSubmodule (average α) :=
  ⟨average_mem_fixedPoints α, fun _ h => average_eq_self h⟩

omit [StarRing R] [StarModule R A] in
/-- The average over the action of `ℤ₂` generated by an involutive ⋆-automorphism `e` is
`a ↦ (a + e a) / 2`. -/
lemma average_involutionHom [Invertible (Fintype.card (Multiplicative (ZMod 2)) : R)]
    (e : A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A) (he : e * e = 1) (a : A) :
    average (involutionHom e he) a =
      ⅟(Fintype.card (Multiplicative (ZMod 2)) : R) • (a + e a) := by
  rw [average_apply, Fintype.sum_eq_add 1 (Multiplicative.ofAdd 1) (by decide), map_one,
    involutionHom_ofAdd_one, one_apply]
  intro x hx
  exfalso
  rcases (by decide : ∀ a : ZMod 2, a = 0 ∨ a = 1) x.toAdd with h | h
  · exact hx.1 (by rw [← ofAdd_toAdd x, h, ofAdd_zero])
  · exact hx.2 (by rw [← ofAdd_toAdd x, h])

end Average

section CStarAlgebra

variable {G : Type*} [Monoid G]

/-- The fixed-point algebra of an action by ⋆-automorphisms of a C⋆-algebra that need not be unital
is closed, each of them being isometric; it is a C⋆-algebra. -/
instance instIsClosedNonUnitalFixedPoints {A : Type*} [NonUnitalCStarAlgebra A]
    (α : G →* (A ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] A)) : IsClosed (nonUnitalFixedPoints α : Set A) :=
  isClosed_nonUnitalFixedPoints α fun g => (isometry (α g)).continuous

variable {A : Type*} [CStarAlgebra A]

/-- The fixed-point algebra of an action by ⋆-automorphisms of a C⋆-algebra is closed, each of them
being isometric. With `StarSubalgebra.cstarAlgebra`, it is a C⋆-algebra. -/
instance instIsClosedFixedPoints (α : G →* (A ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] A)) : IsClosed (fixedPoints α : Set A) :=
  instIsClosedNonUnitalFixedPoints α

/-- **The fixed points of the inner action are the centre**: `u x u⋆ = x` for every unitary `u`
iff `x` is central. One direction is `u x = x u` for every unitary `u`; the unitaries span `A`
(`CStarAlgebra.span_unitary`), so `x` commutes with all of `A`. -/
theorem fixedPoints_conjStarAlgAut :
    (fixedPoints (Unitary.conjStarAlgAut ℂ A)).toSubalgebra = Subalgebra.center ℂ A := by
  ext x
  simp only [StarSubalgebra.mem_toSubalgebra, mem_fixedPoints, Unitary.conjStarAlgAut_apply,
    Subalgebra.mem_center_iff]
  constructor
  · intro h y
    have hu (u : unitary A) : (u : A) * x = x * u :=
      calc (u : A) * x = u * x * (star (u : A) * u) := by simp
        _ = (u * x * star (u : A)) * u := by noncomm_ring
        _ = x * u := by rw [h u]
    have hle : Submodule.span ℂ (unitary A : Set A) ≤
        Subalgebra.toSubmodule (Subalgebra.centralizer ℂ {x}) := by
      rw [Submodule.span_le]
      intro u hu'
      simp only [SetLike.mem_coe, Subalgebra.mem_toSubmodule, Subalgebra.mem_centralizer_iff,
        Set.mem_singleton_iff, forall_eq]
      exact (hu ⟨u, hu'⟩).symm
    have hy := hle (CStarAlgebra.span_unitary A ▸ Submodule.mem_top (x := y))
    simp only [Subalgebra.mem_toSubmodule, Subalgebra.mem_centralizer_iff, Set.mem_singleton_iff,
      forall_eq] at hy
    exact hy.symm
  · intro h u
    rw [h, mul_assoc]
    simp

end CStarAlgebra

section Restriction

variable {G R A S : Type*} [Group G] [Add A] [Mul A] [SMul R A] [Star A]
  [SetLike S A] [AddMemClass S A] [MulMemClass S A] [SMulMemClass S R A] [StarMemClass S A]

/-- The **restriction** of a ⋆-automorphism `e` to a ⋆-subalgebra `s` that `e` and `e.symm` map
into itself. Neither `A` nor `s` need be unital. -/
def restrict (e : A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A) (s : S) (h : ∀ x ∈ s, e x ∈ s) (h' : ∀ x ∈ s, e.symm x ∈ s) :
    s ≃⋆ₐ[R] s where
  toFun x := ⟨e x, h x x.2⟩
  invFun x := ⟨e.symm x, h' x x.2⟩
  left_inv x := Subtype.ext (e.symm_apply_apply x)
  right_inv x := Subtype.ext (e.apply_symm_apply x)
  map_mul' x y := Subtype.ext <| map_mul e (x : A) y
  map_add' x y := Subtype.ext <| map_add e (x : A) y
  map_smul' r x := Subtype.ext <| map_smul e r (x : A)
  map_star' x := Subtype.ext <| map_star e (x : A)

/-- The restriction agrees with `e` on `s`. -/
@[simp] lemma coe_restrict_apply (e : A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A) (s : S) (h : ∀ x ∈ s, e x ∈ s)
    (h' : ∀ x ∈ s, e.symm x ∈ s) (x : s) : (restrict e s h h' x : A) = e x :=
  rfl

/-- The **restriction** of an action `α : G →* (A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A)` to a ⋆-subalgebra `s` invariant under
every `α g`: each `α g` maps `s` onto itself, its inverse `α g⁻¹` preserving `s` as well. Neither `A`
nor `s` need be unital, so `s` may be an invariant ideal spelled as a `NonUnitalStarSubalgebra`. -/
def restrictHom (α : G →* (A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A)) (s : S) (h : ∀ g, ∀ x ∈ s, α g x ∈ s) :
    G →* (s ≃⋆ₐ[R] s) where
  toFun g := restrict (α g) s (h g) fun x hx => by
    have := h g⁻¹ x hx
    rw [map_inv] at this
    exact this
  map_one' := by
    ext
    simp
  map_mul' g g' := by
    ext
    simp

/-- The restricted action agrees with `α` on `s`. -/
@[simp] lemma coe_restrictHom_apply (α : G →* (A ≃⋆ₐ[R] A)) (s : S) (h : ∀ g, ∀ x ∈ s, α g x ∈ s)
    (g : G) (x : s) : (restrictHom α s h g x : A) = α g x :=
  rfl

end Restriction

end StarAlgEquiv

namespace ContinuousMap

variable (G X : Type*) [Group G] [TopologicalSpace G] [ContinuousInv G] [TopologicalSpace X]
  [MulAction G X] [ContinuousSMul G X]

/-- A group `G` with continuous inversion acting continuously on a space `X` acts on the continuous functions
`C(X, ℂ)` by `(g · f) x = f (g⁻¹ • x)`, continuously for the topology of pointwise convergence on
the ⋆-automorphisms of `C(X, ℂ)` with the compact-open topology. For a compact `X` that topology is
the norm topology and this is a C⋆-dynamical system on the commutative C⋆-algebra `C(X, ℂ)`; `G`
need not be discrete, as for the rotations `ContinuousMap.smulStarAlgAut Circle Circle` of
the circle. -/
noncomputable def smulStarAlgAut : G →ₜ* (C(X, ℂ) ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] C(X, ℂ)) where
  toFun g := (Homeomorph.smul g⁻¹).compStarAlgEquiv' ℂ ℂ
  map_one' := by
    ext f x
    simp
  map_mul' g h := by
    ext f x
    simp [mul_smul]
  continuous_toFun := StarAlgEquiv.continuous_iff.mpr fun f =>
    ContinuousMap.continuous_of_continuous_uncurry _ <| by
      change Continuous fun p : G × X => f (p.1⁻¹ • p.2)
      fun_prop

variable {G X}

/-- The action on functions is `(g · f) x = f (g⁻¹ • x)`. -/
@[simp] lemma smulStarAlgAut_apply (g : G) (f : C(X, ℂ)) (x : X) :
    smulStarAlgAut G X g f x = f (g⁻¹ • x) :=
  rfl

/-- The fixed points of the action of `G` on `C(X, ℂ)` are the `G`-invariant functions. -/
lemma mem_fixedPoints_smulStarAlgAut {f : C(X, ℂ)} :
    f ∈ StarAlgEquiv.fixedPoints (smulStarAlgAut G X).toMonoidHom ↔
      ∀ (g : G) (x : X), f (g • x) = f x := by
  rw [StarAlgEquiv.mem_fixedPoints]
  refine ⟨fun h g x => ?_, fun h g => ?_⟩
  · have hx := DFunLike.congr_fun (h g⁻¹) x
    change f ((g⁻¹)⁻¹ • x) = f x at hx
    rwa [inv_inv] at hx
  · ext x
    exact h g⁻¹ x

/-- **For a transitive action, the fixed points are the constants**: the fixed-point algebra of the
action of `G` on `C(X, ℂ)` is `⊥`, the scalar multiples of `1`. -/
theorem fixedPoints_smulStarAlgAut_of_isPretransitive [MulAction.IsPretransitive G X] :
    StarAlgEquiv.fixedPoints (smulStarAlgAut G X).toMonoidHom = ⊥ := by
  refine eq_bot_iff.mpr fun f hf => ?_
  rw [mem_fixedPoints_smulStarAlgAut] at hf
  rw [StarSubalgebra.mem_bot]
  rcases isEmpty_or_nonempty X with hX | ⟨⟨x₀⟩⟩
  · exact ⟨0, by ext x; exact (hX.false x).elim⟩
  · refine ⟨f x₀, ?_⟩
    ext x
    obtain ⟨g, rfl⟩ := MulAction.exists_smul_eq G x₀ x
    simp [hf g x₀]

end ContinuousMap
